WEBVTT

00:00:02.919 --> 00:00:04.212
A Halloween event?

00:00:04.212 --> 00:00:07.674
Yes. You all know what
Halloween is, don't you?

00:00:07.674 --> 00:00:10.385
That holiday with all the pumpkin
decorations, like they have here?

00:00:10.385 --> 00:00:11.094
That's right.

00:00:11.553 --> 00:00:16.808
There's going to be a Halloween
street event in Akiba this year.

00:00:16.808 --> 00:00:21.938
They have asked the local school idol
groups, A-RISE and p's, to perform.

00:00:21.938 --> 00:00:27.110
Really? Since passing the preliminaries,
it's amazing what we're getting to do.

00:00:27.110 --> 00:00:28.903
Will it involve singing?

00:00:29.279 --> 00:00:30.572
Seems like it.

00:00:30.572 --> 00:00:33.867
I'm grateful for the opportunity, but
should we keep doing events like this

00:00:33.867 --> 00:00:35.910
and that fashion show?

00:00:35.910 --> 00:00:37.787
The final preliminaries are coming up.

00:00:37.787 --> 00:00:42.000
Yeah. Isn't our goal to win Love Live?

00:00:42.000 --> 00:00:45.462
Yes, but we need to take
these small steps, too.

00:00:46.421 --> 00:00:49.382
The event's going to be
covered by a TV station.

00:00:49.841 --> 00:00:50.759
TVI?

00:00:50.759 --> 00:00:52.302
You changed your tune quickly.

00:00:52.302 --> 00:00:56.014
If we're performing with A-RISE,
everyone's attention will be on us.

00:00:56.014 --> 00:00:57.682
I'm so nervous.

00:00:57.682 --> 00:01:00.727
But it's a great opportunity to gain exposure.

00:01:00.727 --> 00:01:04.397
That's right! By giving a more
impactful performance than A-RISE,

00:01:04.397 --> 00:01:08.568
we're going to burn our existence
into the audience's brains!

00:01:09.986 --> 00:01:12.656
Maki-chan, we need to focus on impact now!

00:01:14.032 --> 00:01:15.825
By the way, Honoka...

00:01:17.077 --> 00:01:19.829
Should you even be here?

00:01:19.829 --> 00:01:21.831
What about your student
council president duties?

00:01:24.668 --> 00:01:26.211
How do you do?

00:01:26.211 --> 00:01:28.546
W-We've been looking for you.

00:01:29.255 --> 00:01:33.259
Really? We need to focus on impact, do we?

00:01:36.596 --> 00:01:39.057
This isn't the kind of impact I wanted.

00:01:39.057 --> 00:01:45.271
Saa yume wo kanaeru no wa minna no yuuki Come
on... Our courage makes our dreams come true

00:01:45.271 --> 00:01:52.862
makenai (kokoro de) ashita e kaketeyukou Let's
run toward tomorrow with unbeaten (hearts)

00:01:59.911 --> 00:02:05.250
Tsuyoi tsuyoi negaigoto ga
A strong, strong wish

00:02:05.250 --> 00:02:10.797
bokutachi wo michibiite kureta
Led us along

00:02:10.797 --> 00:02:15.885
tsugi wa zettai yuzurenaiyo
We can't give up the next one

00:02:15.885 --> 00:02:21.057
nokosareta jikan wo nigirishimete We'll hold
on tightly to the time we have remaining

00:02:21.057 --> 00:02:26.521
tada no omoide sore dake ja iyadayo
We don't want only a memory

00:02:26.521 --> 00:02:32.360
seiippai chikara no kagiri hashirunda
We'll run as hard as we can

00:02:32.360 --> 00:02:35.238
(CHANCE FOR ME CHANCE FOR YOU)
(Chance for me! Chance for you!)

00:02:35.238 --> 00:02:40.827
Saa yume wo dakishimetara ue wo muite
Come on... Embrace your dreams and look up

00:02:40.827 --> 00:02:45.665
kimi no sekai ga ohkiku kawaruyo
Your world will change dramatically

00:02:45.665 --> 00:02:51.755
saa yume wo kanaeru no wa minna no yuuki Come
on... Our courage makes our dreams come true

00:02:51.755 --> 00:02:56.801
makenai (kokoro de) ashita e kaketeyukou Let's
run toward tomorrow with unbeaten (hearts)

00:02:56.801 --> 00:03:02.140
Ima koko de deaeta kiseki
The miracle that we met here and now

00:03:02.140 --> 00:03:08.855
wasurenaide bokutachi no kisetsu
Don't forget our season

00:03:11.107 --> 00:03:13.067
#6 - Happy Halloween
Impact, huh?

00:03:13.067 --> 00:03:16.279
But this isn't a competition, right?

00:03:16.279 --> 00:03:20.450
We won't be compared, so you
don't need to worry about it.

00:03:20.450 --> 00:03:21.910
You're right.

00:03:21.910 --> 00:03:23.161
What are you talking about!?

00:03:23.161 --> 00:03:25.079
The battle has already begun!

00:03:25.079 --> 00:03:27.248
Nico-chan's right.

00:03:27.248 --> 00:03:29.918
There won't be a score or rankings, but

00:03:29.918 --> 00:03:33.713
whoever leaves a bigger impression on the
audience will probably get more coverage.

00:03:33.713 --> 00:03:35.507
And they'll remember us, too.

00:03:35.507 --> 00:03:36.591
I see.

00:03:36.591 --> 00:03:37.425
Yes, yes.

00:03:37.425 --> 00:03:40.470
In other words, it'll help us
in the final preliminaries!

00:03:40.470 --> 00:03:41.721
That's right.

00:03:41.721 --> 00:03:44.724
On top of that, A-RISE has won before.

00:03:44.724 --> 00:03:48.019
They have a staggering lead over
us when it comes to impression.

00:03:48.019 --> 00:03:51.481
And while we have such
important things to discuss...

00:03:51.481 --> 00:03:53.316
What do you think you're doing!?

00:03:53.316 --> 00:03:55.735
I-1 thought it'd put us in
the mood for Halloween.

00:03:55.735 --> 00:03:57.445
Trick or treat.

00:03:59.364 --> 00:04:04.327
Even if we do the same thing, as the
previous winners, they have the advantage.

00:04:04.327 --> 00:04:07.789
A-RISE is sure to be covered
by the media first.

00:04:07.789 --> 00:04:10.708
Are you saying we're at a disadvantage?

00:04:10.708 --> 00:04:12.168
That is what that means.

00:04:12.168 --> 00:04:15.463
That's why, in order to close the
gap before the final preliminaries,

00:04:15.463 --> 00:04:18.675
we have to put on an
impressive performance.

00:04:18.675 --> 00:04:20.760
In other words, this will be a prelude.

00:04:21.511 --> 00:04:22.428
How cute.

00:04:22.428 --> 00:04:22.971
What?

00:04:23.638 --> 00:04:25.014
A prelude...

00:04:25.014 --> 00:04:28.393
But in order to leave a deeper
impression than A-RISE...

00:04:28.393 --> 00:04:29.727
How can we do that?

00:04:29.727 --> 00:04:32.021
I've told you plenty of times.

00:04:33.481 --> 00:04:36.484
The most important thing is having impact!

00:04:36.985 --> 00:04:38.945
Alright! So here we have it!

00:04:38.945 --> 00:04:39.487
Yeah!

00:04:39.696 --> 00:04:42.782
The Akiba Halloween
Festival began today!

00:04:42.782 --> 00:04:45.326
To everyone watching this
broadcast are you cutting loose?

00:04:45.952 --> 00:04:49.289
She has more impact than we do.

00:04:49.289 --> 00:04:51.249
She's definitely cutting loose.

00:04:51.749 --> 00:04:54.794
As you can see, the event is in full swing.

00:04:54.794 --> 00:04:57.130
Lots of people are having fun in costume.

00:04:57.130 --> 00:04:58.923
You can still make it in time.

00:04:59.257 --> 00:05:00.884
And would you believe it?

00:05:00.884 --> 00:05:05.305
On the final day, school idols will
be performing a concert for us!

00:05:05.847 --> 00:05:07.599
Yahoo! Are you girls cutting loose?

00:05:07.599 --> 00:05:08.224
Uh, yeah.

00:05:08.683 --> 00:05:11.019
Show us your enthusiasm for the concert.

00:05:11.019 --> 00:05:13.229
W-We'll do our best.

00:05:13.229 --> 00:05:16.149
All right, let's hear what you have to say, too.

00:05:16.149 --> 00:05:17.567
We'll do our best at the concert.

00:05:17.567 --> 00:05:19.277
How cute!

00:05:19.277 --> 00:05:20.945
Me, too! Nico-Nico—

00:05:21.404 --> 00:05:25.325
And that's all from the
Otonokizaka High's school idol group.

00:05:25.700 --> 00:05:27.410
And can you believe it?

00:05:28.703 --> 00:05:32.123
A-RISE is participating in the concert, too!

00:05:32.457 --> 00:05:38.463
Every day, we try new things,
so that we can continue to evolve.

00:05:38.463 --> 00:05:43.259
We'd like to shatter our image in a
good way at this Halloween event.

00:05:47.221 --> 00:05:49.057
Happy Halloween!

00:05:53.102 --> 00:05:55.355
Can you believe it!?

00:05:55.355 --> 00:05:56.940
I wouldn't expect any less from A-RISE!

00:05:56.940 --> 00:05:59.317
What an amazing impact!

00:05:59.943 --> 00:06:03.363
You won't be able to take your
eyes off this Halloween event!

00:06:10.203 --> 00:06:11.287
Sheesh.

00:06:11.287 --> 00:06:13.790
A-RISE completely stole the show.

00:06:13.790 --> 00:06:16.250
It's your fault for doing your Nico-Ni bit.

00:06:16.250 --> 00:06:17.335
I didn't even get to do it!

00:06:17.335 --> 00:06:18.586
Yeah.

00:06:20.088 --> 00:06:21.589
In any case, this is a problem.

00:06:22.006 --> 00:06:27.428
If we don't take this Halloween event, we'll
have trouble winning at the final preliminary.

00:06:27.428 --> 00:06:30.264
You saw how excited the guests were.

00:06:30.264 --> 00:06:31.182
You're right.

00:06:31.182 --> 00:06:33.476
You're right. I understand.

00:06:33.476 --> 00:06:35.311
Despite their track record,

00:06:35.311 --> 00:06:37.563
they're not satisfied with their current
situation, and keep improving.

00:06:37.563 --> 00:06:38.523
Yeah, yeah.

00:06:38.523 --> 00:06:41.234
No wonder they won.

00:06:41.234 --> 00:06:42.193
Yep, yep.

00:06:42.193 --> 00:06:44.904
But it's over if you let that impress you!

00:06:44.904 --> 00:06:47.407
I know!

00:06:47.407 --> 00:06:49.617
What are you reading?

00:06:51.202 --> 00:06:53.621
Impact, impact...

00:06:53.621 --> 00:06:57.291
I don't think it's possible for us
to suddenly change our style.

00:06:57.291 --> 00:07:00.211
We don't have enough impact right now!

00:07:00.211 --> 00:07:06.134
But impact comes from doing
new things, doesn't it?

00:07:06.134 --> 00:07:07.969
New things, huh?

00:07:10.805 --> 00:07:15.393
In that case, maybe we should start by
changing the atmosphere around here.

00:07:16.185 --> 00:07:16.894
Atmosphere?

00:07:17.979 --> 00:07:19.939
Lately, I've been thinking...

00:07:19.939 --> 00:07:23.693
It seems like because it's been a
while since we formed our group,

00:07:23.693 --> 00:07:26.904
we now feel secure and
have grown a little lazy.

00:07:26.904 --> 00:07:28.364
You think so?

00:07:28.364 --> 00:07:32.326
I think everyone's excited with
the final preliminaries coming up.

00:07:32.326 --> 00:07:37.248
And where was that someone when she
had to perform her student council duties?

00:07:38.541 --> 00:07:40.209
That's what I'm talking about.

00:07:41.836 --> 00:07:44.464
If we're going to do this, we have to change.

00:07:44.922 --> 00:07:46.966
But how can we do that?

00:07:48.009 --> 00:07:50.511
Well, for example...

00:07:51.721 --> 00:07:53.806
The ace of returning your feelings!

00:07:53.806 --> 00:07:55.099
I'm Kosaka Honokal!

00:07:56.017 --> 00:07:57.810
Driving you crazy with
my ribbon of temptation!

00:07:58.853 --> 00:07:59.854
I'm Nishikino Maki!

00:08:00.396 --> 00:08:03.941
Don't peel me! I'm not ripe yet!

00:08:03.941 --> 00:08:05.526
I'm Koizumi Hanayo!

00:08:06.152 --> 00:08:09.238
I'm the Spiritual Witch of
the East, Tojo Nozomi!

00:08:09.614 --> 00:08:11.699
My chemical formula fell short of love!

00:08:11.699 --> 00:08:12.575
I'm Sonoda Umi!

00:08:13.076 --> 00:08:16.245
I'll cover you in heart-shaped
marks with my shots.

00:08:16.245 --> 00:08:17.163
I'm Minami Kotori!

00:08:17.497 --> 00:08:19.665
Cute splash!

00:08:19.665 --> 00:08:20.666
I'm Hoshizora Rin!

00:08:21.292 --> 00:08:23.294
Deadly pink pompons!

00:08:23.294 --> 00:08:24.170
I'm Ayase Eli!

00:08:25.379 --> 00:08:29.509
And then there's me, the immovable
center, Yazawa Nico-Nico!

00:08:29.967 --> 00:08:33.888
We are the club idol group, (J's!

00:08:40.770 --> 00:08:42.814
You can't even see my face!

00:08:43.439 --> 00:08:45.399
But it's new and refreshing.

00:08:45.399 --> 00:08:46.109
Yeah, yeah.

00:08:46.109 --> 00:08:52.115
Considering we're school idols, it's not a bad
idea for us to wear all kinds of club outfits.

00:08:52.115 --> 00:08:53.533
Yeah, yeah.

00:08:53.533 --> 00:08:56.202
But it seems like...

00:08:56.202 --> 00:08:57.954
We're just messing around!

00:08:57.954 --> 00:08:59.789
- That's not true.
- Swim!

00:08:59.789 --> 00:09:01.666
- Let's do it again.
- Swim!

00:09:01.666 --> 00:09:03.793
- Can I ask you something?
- Swim, swim!

00:09:05.086 --> 00:09:08.923
What club is my outfit
supposed to represent?

00:09:08.923 --> 00:09:10.550
The Science Club!

00:09:10.550 --> 00:09:12.260
What about Hanayo's outfit?

00:09:12.260 --> 00:09:13.553
Probably, the Acting Club.

00:09:13.553 --> 00:09:18.766
We can't go onstage like this.

00:09:18.766 --> 00:09:19.809
You're right.

00:09:20.685 --> 00:09:24.480
What's new about this?

00:09:24.480 --> 00:09:28.109
I'm sorry. It was stupid of me to suggest it.

00:09:28.109 --> 00:09:29.986
But it was kind of fun.

00:09:29.986 --> 00:09:32.697
This isn't the time for that!

00:09:32.697 --> 00:09:36.909
While we're doing this,
A-RISE is evolving every day!

00:09:36.909 --> 00:09:38.286
You're right.

00:09:39.537 --> 00:09:41.581
Something new, something new...

00:09:41.581 --> 00:09:45.459
Wouldn't changing our appearance
be the most obvious way?

00:09:45.459 --> 00:09:47.920
Are you saying we should
wear unconventional outfits?

00:09:49.130 --> 00:09:53.426
That's certainly the quickest way.

00:09:54.051 --> 00:09:55.970
But we just tried that...

00:09:58.764 --> 00:10:03.060
It seems we'll have to see
what the cards have to say.

00:10:08.065 --> 00:10:09.233
Nozomi?

00:10:17.200 --> 00:10:18.618
Love Live!

00:10:21.329 --> 00:10:23.164
Good morning!

00:10:24.332 --> 00:10:25.708
How do you do?

00:10:25.708 --> 00:10:27.168
Umi, khorosho.

00:10:27.168 --> 00:10:29.086
Eli, you're early.

00:10:30.087 --> 00:10:31.547
You, too, Rin.

00:10:36.969 --> 00:10:38.012
I can't!

00:10:38.012 --> 00:10:41.682
No, Umi. You have to be Rin.

00:10:42.308 --> 00:10:46.229
You're the one who suggested
we change the atmosphere.

00:10:46.604 --> 00:10:47.855
Come on, Rin.

00:10:52.777 --> 00:10:57.573
- All right! It's practice time!
- What is that? It doesn't make any sense.

00:10:57.949 --> 00:11:00.660
Maki, don't talk like that.

00:11:00.660 --> 00:11:02.078
You're so annoying.

00:11:02.078 --> 00:11:03.204
Hey, Rin!

00:11:03.204 --> 00:11:05.790
You're copying me, aren't you? Stop that.

00:11:05.790 --> 00:11:06.832
I refuse.

00:11:07.333 --> 00:11:09.252
Good morning, Nozomi.

00:11:11.712 --> 00:11:13.756
It's not fair if you don't talk.

00:11:13.756 --> 00:11:16.133
That's right. We all decided to do this.

00:11:16.133 --> 00:11:18.302
I-I don't...

00:11:19.345 --> 00:11:21.013
...remember agreeing to this.

00:11:21.013 --> 00:11:23.474
Nozomi, that's amazing.

00:11:25.685 --> 00:11:27.561
Nico-Nico-Ni!

00:11:27.561 --> 00:11:30.398
I'll make your heartbeat throb "Nico-Nico-Ni"!

00:11:30.398 --> 00:11:32.942
I'm Yazawa Nico-Nico. I'm here
to make your heart smile!

00:11:32.942 --> 00:11:34.485
Even the blue sky is Nico!

00:11:34.944 --> 00:11:38.197
Khorosho. Nico's more
Nico-like than I expected.

00:11:38.572 --> 00:11:39.490
Nico!

00:11:40.241 --> 00:11:43.369
Nico-chan, Nico isn't like that.

00:11:43.703 --> 00:11:44.662
Kotori.

00:11:45.538 --> 00:11:47.164
The bread tastes delicious again today!

00:11:47.164 --> 00:11:48.833
Honoka, you're late again.

00:11:49.292 --> 00:11:50.334
Sorry.

00:11:50.334 --> 00:11:52.628
Is this what I'm like?

00:11:52.628 --> 00:11:53.421
Yes.

00:11:54.255 --> 00:11:56.007
It's an emergency!

00:11:56.507 --> 00:11:57.800
What's wrong?

00:12:02.096 --> 00:12:03.472
E-Everyone is...

00:12:06.851 --> 00:12:10.021
Everyone is...

00:12:10.604 --> 00:12:11.314
...acting weird.

00:12:13.357 --> 00:12:14.483
You're right.

00:12:17.320 --> 00:12:18.863
This isn't good.

00:12:19.280 --> 00:12:21.949
We're running out of time.

00:12:21.949 --> 00:12:25.745
We failed to change anything.

00:12:25.745 --> 00:12:28.497
I had a thought.

00:12:28.497 --> 00:12:33.252
Why don't we try moving away from idols?

00:12:33.627 --> 00:12:36.005
You mean not acting like idols?

00:12:36.005 --> 00:12:38.049
Like being cool instead?

00:12:38.049 --> 00:12:39.633
Oh, good idea.

00:12:40.009 --> 00:12:43.387
What is being cool like, though?

00:12:43.387 --> 00:12:44.889
Like rock?

00:12:45.264 --> 00:12:47.683
Something wilder?

00:12:47.683 --> 00:12:51.896
Doing something new means
fundamentally changing your image.

00:12:52.855 --> 00:12:54.357
Which means...

00:12:55.441 --> 00:12:56.942
Are we really doing this?

00:12:56.942 --> 00:12:59.820
What are you afraid of now?

00:12:59.820 --> 00:13:02.365
We need to see how people will respond first.

00:13:02.782 --> 00:13:04.992
Okay, let's go.

00:13:10.998 --> 00:13:13.459
It's been a while, everyone.

00:13:13.459 --> 00:13:16.796
We're the school idol group, U's.

00:13:17.171 --> 00:13:21.425
Today, we're overthrowing our
image with anarchy and punk.

00:13:22.301 --> 00:13:26.013
Come see the new face of J's!

00:13:28.641 --> 00:13:29.767
Teacher!

00:13:30.976 --> 00:13:33.062
This seems to have a huge impact.

00:13:33.062 --> 00:13:34.605
This might work.

00:13:35.064 --> 00:13:37.942
Members of the Idol Study Club, u's.

00:13:37.942 --> 00:13:40.528
Please come to the director's
office immediately.

00:13:40.528 --> 00:13:41.445
I repeat...

00:13:45.574 --> 00:13:47.618
Could you explain yourselves?

00:13:47.618 --> 00:13:49.703
Uh, um...

00:13:50.413 --> 00:13:51.747
Why did this happen?

00:13:51.747 --> 00:13:53.124
You don't remember?

00:13:54.625 --> 00:13:59.004
Director, it's not what you think!
We weren't just playing around!

00:13:59.922 --> 00:14:00.965
It's true.

00:14:00.965 --> 00:14:06.303
We were discussing ways to
make it all the way to Love Live.

00:14:06.303 --> 00:14:08.639
If we let ourselves get stuck in
what we've always been doing,

00:14:08.639 --> 00:14:11.684
we won't be able to produce anything new.

00:14:11.684 --> 00:14:14.937
That's right! We were being serious!

00:14:14.937 --> 00:14:16.939
It's unthinkable for you to be angry with us!

00:14:16.939 --> 00:14:18.023
That's right, that's right!

00:14:19.442 --> 00:14:22.862
In any case, I can't accept
that we're in trouble!

00:14:24.405 --> 00:14:25.656
I understand.

00:14:25.656 --> 00:14:28.951
So you're performing at the final
preliminaries like that, then?

00:14:28.951 --> 00:14:30.035
What?

00:14:30.035 --> 00:14:34.999
If so, then I'll allow you to continue
operating in those outfits.

00:14:36.041 --> 00:14:37.543
Uh...

00:14:38.961 --> 00:14:40.713
We're so sorry!

00:14:41.213 --> 00:14:42.756
How did this happen!?

00:14:42.756 --> 00:14:48.512
She's right. I thought we were seriously
discussing how we could have more impact.

00:14:48.512 --> 00:14:50.514
It started with you.

00:14:50.514 --> 00:14:52.766
You said we should try
dressing like various clubs.

00:14:52.766 --> 00:14:53.809
I...

00:14:54.268 --> 00:14:57.104
But then it was the rest of you.

00:14:57.104 --> 00:14:58.814
Yes, but...

00:14:58.814 --> 00:15:01.650
We decided to do it together.

00:15:01.650 --> 00:15:04.778
Blaming each other won't do any good.

00:15:05.112 --> 00:15:11.076
You're right. Maybe we should focus
on how we're actually going to dress.

00:15:11.076 --> 00:15:12.119
You're right.

00:15:14.538 --> 00:15:15.539
Kotori-chan?

00:15:16.957 --> 00:15:23.255
I've been thinking about it, and I want to
create something that suits everyone.

00:15:24.173 --> 00:15:26.550
I don't think we should
focus so much on impact.

00:15:27.384 --> 00:15:29.220
But then we can't beat A-RISE!

00:15:42.024 --> 00:15:43.859
What should we do?

00:15:43.859 --> 00:15:46.070
Let's think about it tomorrow.

00:15:46.070 --> 00:15:49.823
In any case, we have to at least
start working on costumes.

00:15:49.823 --> 00:15:51.825
Huh? Where's Honoka-chan?

00:15:56.205 --> 00:15:58.457
Honoka, you're gonna be left behind.

00:15:58.999 --> 00:15:59.583
Oh, sorry.

00:16:00.834 --> 00:16:06.090
Halloween seems different at night
than during the day, doesn't it?

00:16:08.342 --> 00:16:10.469
It's beautiful.

00:16:10.469 --> 00:16:13.305
Let's go. It's getting late.

00:16:13.305 --> 00:16:14.014
Okay.

00:16:21.146 --> 00:16:23.691
I'm sorry. I made a mistake.

00:16:24.733 --> 00:16:26.569
This doesn't seem right.

00:16:27.945 --> 00:16:30.281
Why are we making the costumes?

00:16:31.073 --> 00:16:34.285
Everyone else is busy preparing
for the concert in other ways.

00:16:34.285 --> 00:16:35.536
Yeah, right.

00:16:36.036 --> 00:16:39.206
They just wasted a bunch
of time on nonsense.

00:16:39.790 --> 00:16:42.668
I don't think it was a complete waste.

00:16:42.668 --> 00:16:43.669
Huh? What do you mean?

00:16:44.378 --> 00:16:46.547
I had fun.

00:16:46.547 --> 00:16:49.258
And it gave me some design ideas.

00:16:49.592 --> 00:16:51.468
Being in charge of costume design,

00:16:51.468 --> 00:16:53.262
are you sure you're not just
used to doing the lame jobs?

00:16:56.307 --> 00:16:58.767
I have my responsibilities.

00:16:59.727 --> 00:17:01.478
It's always been this way.

00:17:01.979 --> 00:17:06.942
I always want to support whatever
everyone else decides or wants to do.

00:17:06.942 --> 00:17:13.240
Sometimes we might lose our way,
but I don't think it's a complete waste.

00:17:14.867 --> 00:17:16.744
This is your costume.

00:17:18.329 --> 00:17:25.628
If we all come together and do our jobs, don't
you think a wonderful future's waiting for us?

00:17:33.177 --> 00:17:35.679
Trick or treat!

00:17:35.679 --> 00:17:38.015
Yahoo! Are you cutting loose?

00:17:38.015 --> 00:17:41.977
We've been covering the hype over the
Akiba Halloween Festival the last few days!

00:17:41.977 --> 00:17:44.563
Everyone's been coming out
to turn up the excitement!

00:17:44.563 --> 00:17:47.650
However, today is the final
day of the event. Too bad.

00:17:47.650 --> 00:17:53.113
But don't be sad. Today, you'll get to
see a special school idol concert!

00:17:53.113 --> 00:17:54.156
Don't miss it!

00:17:55.115 --> 00:17:58.535
The concert's finally here. I'm so nervous.

00:17:58.535 --> 00:18:00.287
Let's try to enjoy it.

00:18:01.038 --> 00:18:03.248
Look. Everyone seems to be having fun.

00:18:04.333 --> 00:18:07.461
Look! It's a huge pumpkin!

00:18:07.461 --> 00:18:09.129
Yeah.

00:18:09.129 --> 00:18:11.340
It's so big.

00:18:16.178 --> 00:18:17.971
I've never seen one this big before!

00:18:19.223 --> 00:18:20.265
What's wrong?

00:18:21.100 --> 00:18:22.226
Nothing.

00:18:23.560 --> 00:18:24.603
Hey, Eli-chan...

00:18:26.438 --> 00:18:29.483
I think we're just fine the way we are.

00:18:29.483 --> 00:18:35.447
We tried reinventing ourselves
since A-RISE is so amazing.

00:18:35.447 --> 00:18:39.451
But I think we're best the way we are now.

00:18:40.202 --> 00:18:42.746
After all, everyone's unique.

00:18:44.415 --> 00:18:50.170
Normal high school students hang out with
people like themselves, but we're different.

00:18:51.046 --> 00:18:56.135
We took the time to get to know
each other, and accept each other.

00:18:56.135 --> 00:18:57.678
That's how we made it this far.

00:18:58.512 --> 00:19:02.057
Don't you think that's our strongest trait?

00:19:02.891 --> 00:19:04.768
That's what I like about p's.

00:19:06.520 --> 00:19:08.480
Yeah, me too!

00:19:51.023 --> 00:19:52.900
ITS A MAGICAL
It's a magical

00:19:52.900 --> 00:19:57.696
fushigi ga guuzen wo maneiteru
Is magic inviting coincidences?

00:19:57.696 --> 00:20:05.037
Aetano wa aetano wa sutekina unmei
We met, we met because of a wonderful fate

